## 4. Existing dark mode support — essentially none

Only two hits across the entire codebase:

- `app/globals.css:5` — `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));`
- `app/globals.css:128` — the `.dark { … }` token block

There is **zero** usage of:
- the `dark:` variant in any `.tsx` file (0 occurrences)
- `prefers-color-scheme` (0)
- `data-theme` (0)
- `next-themes` (not in `package.json`)
- any code that adds/removes the `.dark` class

So the `.dark` block is **dead code that has never been rendered**. It is, however, already written and reasonable — it's the natural starting point. Its remap:

| Token | light | `.dark` |
|---|---|---|
| `--background` | `#f5f1e8` (ivory) | `#141414` (charcoal) |
| `--foreground` | charcoal | ivory |
| `--card` / `--popover` | `#faf8f2` | `#1a1a1a` (charcoal-2) |
| `--primary` / `-foreground` | charcoal / ivory | ivory / charcoal |
| `--secondary` / `--muted` | cream | `#242424` |
| `--muted-foreground` | `--stone` `#6b6b6b` | `--stone-2` `#9a9a9a` |
| `--accent` | `--gold` `#b99c6b` | `--gold-soft` `#c9ae7c` |
| `--destructive` | `#8f2f2f` | `#c96a6a` |
| `--border` | `#ddd5c5` | `rgb(245 241 232 / 12%)` |
| `--input` | `#ddd5c5` | `rgb(245 241 232 / 16%)` |
| `--ring` | `--bronze` | `--gold-soft` |

Note the `.dark` block does **not** override `--bronze`. `text-bronze` (#7a5a33, the single most-used accent, 64 uses) would sit at roughly **1.9:1 on #141414** — a hard WCAG failure. This is the #1 remap decision.

