## 6. Layout components — light-background assumptions

### `/home/cis/windows/realstate/components/layout/site-header.tsx` (client)
Fixed, `z-50`, `h-20`, transitions on `--ease-transition`. Two visual states driven by `solid = scrolled || menuOpen || !overDarkHero`, where `overDarkHero = useSelectedLayoutSegment() === null` (home only).

```
solid  ? "bg-background text-foreground border-b border-border"
       : "text-ivory bg-transparent"
```
Nav links: `solid ? "text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground" : "text-ivory/75 hover:text-ivory"`.
Enquire button: `border border-current`, `solid ? "hover:bg-foreground hover:text-background" : "hover:bg-ivory hover:text-charcoal"`.
Mobile sheet: `bg-background border-t border-border`, items `border-b border-border`.

**Dark impact:** the header is mostly theme-aware and converts cleanly. But the whole `solid` / transparent duality **collapses** — on a dark page the transparent-over-hero state and the solid state look nearly identical. The two-state logic becomes decorative; consider swapping the differentiator from colour to `backdrop-blur` + hairline border. Also, `bg-background` with no opacity means the solid header is fully opaque charcoal over a charcoal page — the `border-b border-border` (12% ivory) becomes the only separator.

### `/home/cis/windows/realstate/components/layout/site-footer.tsx` (server)
`<footer className="bg-charcoal text-ivory mt-auto">`. Internally already fully dark: `text-stone-2` for secondary copy (lines 19, 29, 45, 66, 77, 111), `text-gold-soft` for column headings and the RERA number (28, 56, 105), `hover:text-ivory` transitions (84, 111), and a `border-white/10` statutory divider (53).

**Dark impact:** this is the *only* component that already reads correctly in the target theme. **It is effectively the design reference for the dark conversion** — the charcoal/stone-2/gold-soft/white-10 recipe here is what the rest of the site should adopt. Risk: once the page body is also charcoal, the footer no longer visually separates from `main`; it will need an explicit top border or a tonal step (charcoal-2).

### `/home/cis/windows/realstate/components/layout/festive-banner.tsx` (server)
Renders `null` unless `siteConfig.festiveOffer.active`. Root: `<aside className="bg-forest text-ivory">`, inner `container-page … py-4`, label `text-small`, link `eyebrow border-b border-current pb-1 shrink-0`.

**Dark impact:** `--forest #243b34` against `--charcoal #141414` is a ~1.5:1 tonal step — the banner nearly vanishes. Forest needs lightening or replacing with gold/bronze for this strip. Note: rendered *after* `SiteHeader` in the layout, and the header is `fixed`, so the banner sits under the header — check for overlap regardless of theme.

